Lobium — native fingerprint config channel + native surfaces (browser reads file → renderer/browser reads config).

The sidecar writes lobium-fp.json and launches Lobium with --lobium-fp-config=<path>. The BROWSER process
reads the file once (cached; GaiaConfig pattern) and forwards its base64 to each renderer as
--lobium-fp-data (size-guarded). lobium::LobiumFpConfig::Current() (added module //components/lobium_fp,
wired by core/build-gn.patch) parses it once and serves typed fields to every subsystem — in the renderer
AND the browser process (the UA header hook below runs browser-side). Every failure path LOG(ERROR)s so a
present-but-unparseable config never silently leaks the host fingerprint. Config forwarding reaches worker
renderer processes too, so Current() is populated for dedicated/shared/service workers.

Native surfaces (all read Current(); proven on Chromium 152.0.7928.0 — canvas/WebGL/audio/screen proofs
on SwiftShader, real-GPU validation pending):
  • navigator.hardwareConcurrency / deviceMemory (+ Device-Memory client-hint header) / maxTouchPoints
  • navigator.userAgent + navigator.platform in ALL contexts incl. workers (navigator_base.cc)
  • WebGL UNMASKED vendor/renderer (atomic pair) AND per-profile WebGL PIXEL FARBLING (seeds.webgl):
    gl.readPixels (bottom-up) + WebGL toDataURL/toBlob (top-down) farbled Y-flip-COHERENTLY on a shared
    top-down key, so two profiles on the same GPU get distinct-but-stable WebGL pixel hashes and a
    detector cross-checking readPixels vs the encoded image sees consistent noise. Default-framebuffer +
    RGBA/UNSIGNED_BYTE + default-pack only.
  • Canvas 2D farbling (getImageData / toDataURL / toBlob / OffscreenCanvas.convertToBlob), seeds.canvas
  • Web Audio farbling (OfflineAudioContext + analyser + AudioWorklet/ScriptProcessorNode taps), seeds.audio
  • screen geometry / colorDepth / DPR (screen.cc + local_dom_window.cc) + matchMedia DPR (media_values.cc)
  • HTTP User-Agent request header + Sec-CH-UA client-hint metadata (userAgentData), NATIVE, browser-side
    (components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc — GetUserAgent + GetUserAgentMetadata). This is the
    deepest shared UA source, so navigations, subresources, AND all three worker types send the persona UA
    + branded Sec-CH-UA (incl. the "Google Chrome" brand) — closing the worker header leak that the
    per-frame CDP override never reached, and removing the unbranded-Chromium tell natively.

Now NATIVE (previously CDP): the HTTP UA header + UA-CH userAgentData. Only languages + timezone/locale/geo
remain CDP-applied (cdp-fingerprint.ts) — see hooks.md. The CDP UA override is still applied for the
interim (unpatched) Chromium engine and is harmlessly redundant on Lobium (both agree on the persona).

The exact hook points (file + surface) are enumerated in ../hooks.md; the diffs below are the source of
truth. Workers inherit the same --lobium-fp-data forwarded by the render_process_host hook.
